# Exact gitleaks fingerprints (<commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>) to ignore, each with its reason.
#
# CI scans the working tree and the history of HEAD only (.github/workflows/ci.yml): on a
# pull request, the PR's own commits; on main, main's. Pull requests are squash-merged, so
# a fingerprint for a commit of a PR is dead once it merges: remove it then. Prefer the
# allowlisted tok-SENSITIVE- canary prefix (.gitleaks.toml) or a value built at run time.
